A||||3||la9||V6 Valve covers||||5||
Z||000000||la9||02-19-2000||06:40 PM||||Can you get them off without removing the top two plenums ? The book says you can, has anyone done this ?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gokart||02-19-2000||06:55 PM||||Couldn't figure out how to get the one facing the rear of the car off myself after removing all the cover bolts so I brought it into the shop and the mechanic there got it off without removing either plenum. Don't know how the hell he did it though. It felt like there are two protruding metal tabs on each end under the valve cover keeping it from sliding down and off. It's making me wonder if he broke these metal tabs right off and I'm hoping if he did he didn't drop them.||||reg||2
Z||000002||Oreif||02-19-2000||10:45 PM||||The valve covers can be removed but you have to loosen the mounts at both ends of the block and wiggle them out. It is a big pain but can be done. The trick is getting them back on without pinching or gouging the gasket! I have done it but it took me a couple of hours! (and 3 gaskets!)||||reg||1
Z||000003||dogtired||02-20-2000||06:09 AM||||I have replaced valve cover gaskets on both my V6's and have removed the plenums both times   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>It isn't tough and it is a good time to check  the vaccuum lines  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>Good Luck!||||reg||6
